WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:07.600
Weaving and knitting to create fabric are
some of our oldest forms of technology

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.560
Now those ancient practices have become high
tech manufacturing,

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:15.660
and they are meeting up with cutting edge robotics to create artificial muscles

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:21.380
These textile actuators, or textuators, are
made from cellulose yarn.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:27.340
Instead of dye, the yarn is coated with a
material called polypyrrole that moves in response to electricity

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.440
The textuators can be woven or knitted.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:36.040
Woven forms can exert more force, but the
knitted ones can stretch and change shape

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:41.380
The fabric can be tweaked to give the right
balance of stretchiness and strength

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:46.140
This new fabric is designed to be manufactured
at industrial scales.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:53.140
The technology could be integrated into potential
assistive devices like prosthetics or exoskeletons

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:58.560
One day, artificial muscles made of fabric
could be integrated into clothing to aid mobility

